# Typography

Typeface: **IBM Plex Sans** (via `design-system/fonts`). No other family.

## Text roles

| Role | Usage | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| Display | Page titles | `--text-title`, bold |
| Heading | Panel titles | `--text-body`, bold |
| Body | Content | `--text-body` |
| Label / eyebrow | Meta, uppercase eyebrows | `--text-label`, letter-spacing +0.06em |

## Numeric roles (identity carriers)

All product numbers use **tabular figures** (`.dlab-num` pattern:
`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`).

| Role | Size | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Hero numeric | ~3.25rem bold, tight tracking | Overview "Où en est-on ?" reading, Match Hero score / kickoff |
| Row score | ~1.0625rem bold | MatchRow scores |
| Standings points | ~1.0625rem bold | Pts column (dominates the row) |
| Counter | 1.375rem bold + semantic color | À traiter counts |

Rules:
- A match score is always **bigger and bolder** than the team names around it.
- Points dominate a standings row; team name stays regular weight.
- Dates/times are body-size, secondary color — numbers dominate only when they
  are sport-meaningful (score, rank, points, matchday).
